>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC`

``` hol4
simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC :
  simp_mode -> xsimptac_config -> simpset -> thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Globally simplifies a goal under extended fixpoint control.

The configuration type is

``` hol4
type xsimptac_config =
  {base : simptac_config,
   concl_in_fixpoint : bool,
   imp_rebuild : bool}
```

where `simptac_config` is

``` hol4
type simptac_config =
  {strip : bool,
   elimvars : bool,
   droptrues : bool,
   oldestfirst : bool}
```

`GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC mode cfg ss ths` repeatedly simplifies every
assumption using all of the other assumptions, `ths`, and `ss`.  This
reaches a mutual fixpoint, so a rule exposed by a later assumption can
cause an earlier one to be revisited.  Change counting avoids
reprocessing a tail already known to be fixed; this scheduling
optimization does not change the normal result.

The fields of `#base cfg` control processing of each simplified
assumption.  `strip` applies `STRIP_ALL_THEN` when putting it back;
`elimvars` uses an eliminable equality as a variable substitution;
`droptrues` discards an assumption simplified to `T`; and `oldestfirst`
selects the oldest assumption first rather than the newest.

The extra fields control the extent of the fixpoint:

* If `concl_in_fixpoint` is `false`, assumptions first reach their
  fixpoint and the conclusion is then simplified once.  If it is
  `true`, the conclusion is simplified after every assumption pass.  A
  changed or structurally split conclusion restarts the assumption
  pass on each resulting goal.
* If `imp_rebuild` is `true`, the tactic also looks for a root rewrite
  of progressively nested, discharged forms `a ==> w`.  On the first
  hit it replaces that implication, strips its leading implications
  back into assumptions, and restarts the whole fixpoint.  This permits
  implication-left rewrites to rebuild the assumption/conclusion
  structure.  If the field is `false`, this extra root-rewrite search
  is omitted.

The `safe` field of `mode` selects the safe or unsafe final-solver list
for each tactic-level conclusion simplification, both after assumption
passes when `concl_in_fixpoint` is enabled and in the final conclusion
pass.  It does not change rewriting: traversal side conditions continue
to use unsafe solvers, and loopers continue to run.  Simplification of
each individual assumption is conversion-only.  Rewrite markers in
`ths` are processed, and the remaining theorems are available
throughout both the assumption and conclusion phases.

The existing `global_simp_tac base` is equivalent to

``` hol4
simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC
  {safe = false}
  {base = base, concl_in_fixpoint = false, imp_rebuild = false}
```

Thus its conclusion remains outside the mutual fixpoint and implication
rebuilding is disabled by default.

### Failure

The tactic does not fail merely because no simplification is possible,
but it may diverge.  Exceptions from user conversions, loopers, solvers,
or ordering functions may propagate.

### Example

The following schematic configuration enables both extended modes while
using the usual stripping and truth-dropping policy.

``` hol4
val base_cfg =
  {strip = true, elimvars = false,
   droptrues = true, oldestfirst = true}

val extended_global =
  simpLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC
    {safe = false}
    {base = base_cfg,
     concl_in_fixpoint = true,
     imp_rebuild = true}
    bool_ss
```

It can then be applied as `extended_global ths`.

